<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wang Mang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 45 BCE–<a href="/years/23">23 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wang Mang was a Han court official and relative of the empress dowager who seized the throne in 9 CE and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xin-dynasty">Xin dynasty</a>. He attempted sweeping reforms, nationalising land, abolishing private <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> and reissuing coinage. Floods of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-eyebrows">Red Eyebrows</a> revolt followed, and he was killed when rebels took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a> in 23 CE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wang-mang.jpg" alt="Wang Mang" width="320" height="462" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 鍾 惺, 1574-1624 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:WUL-he21_01467_%E6%96%B0%E9%90%AB%E7%B9%AA%E5%83%8F%E6%9D%B1%E8%A5%BF%E6%BC%A2%E5%85%A8%E5%82%B3_01_(%E7%8E%8B%E8%8E%BD).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
